  }
}</pre><article><h2>R1: Inventory hides resources after the first 40 directory entries</h2><p class="status">Implemented; deterministic regressions passed</p><pre>{
  &quot;baseline&quot;: &quot;Manager list_resources truncates before filtering runtime directories, has no cursor, and returns filesystem order.&quot;,
  &quot;fix&quot;: &quot;Sorted inventory, filtering before pagination, paths, resource kinds, byte sizes, explicit scan limits.&quot;,
  &quot;verification&quot;: &quot;test_inventory_pages_past_distractors_and_excludes_runtime&quot;
}</pre></article><article><h2>R2: Large logs are inaccessible and source contents cannot be searched</h2><p class="status">Implemented; deterministic regressions passed</p><pre>{
  &quot;baseline&quot;: &quot;A 198 KiB log with the critical clue at its tail is rejected while planning because sources are capped at 128 KiB.&quot;,
  &quot;fix&quot;: &quot;Streaming revision hashes and bounded, paginated source search and reads, with explicit limits.&quot;,
  &quot;verification&quot;: &quot;test_large_log_tail_is_searchable_and_citable&quot;
}</pre></article><article><h2>R3: No numerical tool compares aggregate cost across metrics</h2><p class="status">Implemented; deterministic regressions passed</p><pre>{
  &quot;baseline&quot;: &quot;Researchers can read short excerpts but cannot aggregate CSV measurements, making frequency and impact easy to confuse.&quot;,
  &quot;fix&quot;: &quot;Paginated CSV aggregation recording counts, sums, ranges, invalid values and incomplete coverage as citable evidence.&quot;,
  &quot;verification&quot;: &quot;test_csv_aggregation_compares_total_cost_instead_of_loudest_warning&quot;
}</pre></article><article><h2>R4: No visible coverage or unexplored frontier for reprioritization</h2><p class="status">Coverage view implemented; live search behavior remains incomplete</p><pre>{
  &quot;baseline&quot;: &quot;Opportunity scores reward evidence confidence; the manager has no concise view of unexamined planned sources, signal classes, or concentration.&quot;,
  &quot;fix&quot;: &quot;Expose observed source coverage, untouched scoped resources, unresolved opportunities and exploration advice; instruct manager to compare alternatives and seek contradictions.&quot;,
  &quot;verification&quot;: &quot;Coverage and manager context tests plus autonomous evaluation harness&quot;
}</pre></article><article><h2>R5: Independent review can approve with citations unrelated to the claims</h2><p class="status">Implemented; deterministic regressions passed</p><pre>{
  &quot;baseline&quot;: &quot;gate returns supported when claim cites db but evaluator cites cache. save_findings leaves it unverified, yet the job remains supported and can enable implementation authorization.&quot;,
  &quot;fix&quot;: &quot;Require evaluator evidence coverage for every factual claim before accepting the job.&quot;,
  &quot;verification&quot;: &quot;test_supported_verdict_must_cover_every_claim_not_an_unrelated_citation&quot;
}</pre></article><article><h2>R6: Duplicate detection can return a different goal&#x27;s job</h2><p class="status">Implemented; deterministic regressions passed</p><pre>{
  &quot;baseline&quot;: &quot;Research signatures omit goal ID despite goal-specific jobs, budgets and acceptance criteria.&quot;,
  &quot;fix&quot;: &quot;Scope duplicate lookup to the current goal while preserving knowledge retrieval across goals.&quot;,
  &quot;verification&quot;: &quot;test_duplicate_investigation_does_not_return_another_goals_job&quot;
}</pre></article><article><h2>R7: No HTML tracking report</h2><p class="status">Implemented; deterministic regressions passed</p><pre>{
  &quot;baseline&quot;: &quot;Only CLI/JSON export exists; no persistent human-readable findings and fix history.&quot;,
  &quot;fix&quot;: &quot;Escaped standalone HTML reports for evaluation history and per-goal evidence/decision logs.&quot;,
  &quot;verification&quot;: &quot;test_html_report_escapes_source_text and CLI export smoke test&quot;
}</pre></article><article><h2>R8: Live research access prerequisites</h2><p class="status">Resolved: credentials propagated and API network access now works</p><pre>{
  &quot;baseline&quot;: &quot;Initially OPENAI_API_KEY was absent, then the egress proxy rejected api.openai.com with CONNECT HTTP 403. These attempts executed no model reasoning.&quot;,
  &quot;fix&quot;: &quot;Reused the secure environment credential after propagation; saved the api.openai.com network addition. Subsequent unauthenticated API probe reached HTTP 401 and actual model trials executed.&quot;,
  &quot;verification&quot;: &quot;live-connected-01 and live-connected-02 contain real manager decisions and specialist reports&quot;
}</pre></article><article><h2>R9: Live manager stops at the first inventory page and underfunds research</h2><p class="status">Partially improved; log-tail coverage and replacement-hypothesis support remain open</p><pre>{
  &quot;baseline&quot;: &quot;Original code: 0/8 checks and premature pause. First tool-improved live case: 0/8 with pause after first 40 entries. Negative control: 3/8; repeated 1-2 call probes sampled cache-only prefixes and never reached decisive code, CSV rows or log tail.&quot;,
  &quot;fix&quot;: &quot;Provide observed root inventory in manager context, surface subdirectory names/counts beyond current page, resolve conflicting delegation guidance, and require budgets suited to whole-file comparisons.&quot;,
  &quot;verification&quot;: &quot;Live iteration 04: 6/8 buried-bottleneck checks, 5/8 negative-control checks. Iteration 05: 5/8 each. Trials are development cases used during tuning, not a held-out estimate.&quot;
}</pre></article><article><h2>R10: Discovery can complete without making a single source observation</h2><p class="status">Reproduced live; guard and tool activation implemented</p><pre>{
  &quot;baseline&quot;: &quot;Iteration 02 produced two discovered reports with zero discretionary tool calls and empty citations, followed by a pause.&quot;,
  &quot;fix&quot;: &quot;Require an initial discovery/research tool call and reject discovery without current observed evidence.&quot;,
  &quot;verification&quot;: &quot;test_discovery_cannot_complete_without_observing_any_evidence; subsequent live trials performed actual source/tool reads.&quot;
}</pre></article><article><h2>R11: Prefix-only metric reasoning and missed log-tail evidence</h2><p class="status">CSV continuation implemented; broader behavioral limitation remains</p><pre>{
  &quot;baseline&quot;: &quot;Live researcher/evaluator treated cache-only CSV prefixes as evidence that other operation types were unmeasured.&quot;,
  &quot;fix&quot;: &quot;Observed CSV column metadata; initial numeric aggregation for numeric CSV scopes; SDK aggregation follows pages within tool budget, preserving incomplete status.&quot;,
  &quot;remaining&quot;: &quot;Some live runs still skip logs, fail to reach decisive log-tail events, or stop after falsification rather than independently verifying the alternative. Do not claim full exploration/exploitation balance.&quot;
}</pre></article><article><h2>R12: Self-audit native worker blocked by masked daemon socket</h2><p class="status">Socket startup resolved; bounded native turns still fail to hand off</p><pre>{
  &quot;baseline&quot;: &quot;Native shells failed because the outer sandbox masks the daemon socket directory. No edits occurred in that attempt; independent oracles failed.&quot;,
  &quot;fix&quot;: &quot;Run self-audit outside the outer command sandbox through the approved execution route; Codex retains its own workspace sandbox.&quot;,
  &quot;verification&quot;: &quot;Supported outer execution route permitted real code edits. Both bounded native attempts timed out; interruption was reconciled and the implementation is escalated. No autonomous completion audit passed.&quot;
}</pre></article><article><h2>R13: Native implementation exceeds its bounded turn without verified completion</h2><p class="status">Reproduced twice; attempt budget exhausted and candidate retained</p><pre>{
  &quot;baseline&quot;: &quot;Self-audit live-03 reached accepted research and real edits but timed out before candidate verification. Latest native usage snapshot: 603768 input tokens (566912 cached), 3869 output tokens. These are cumulative usage values, not unique prompt bytes or a dollar estimate.&quot;,
  &quot;remaining&quot;: &quot;Both native turns reached their 300-second bounds. Final interruption was reconciled and status is escalated. Manual verification of the generated patch is recorded separately; it is not autonomous end-to-end success.&quot;
}</pre></article><article><h2>R14: Evaluation process could exit zero with failed research checkpoints</h2><p class="status">Fixed and regression-tested</p><pre>{
  &quot;baseline&quot;: &quot;The initial harness used exit status only to distinguish runtime exceptions; a completed conversation with 0/8 or 5/8 checks could still exit zero. Those recorded scores remain failures regardless of historical command exit codes.&quot;,
  &quot;fix&quot;: &quot;Exit 0 only for all checkpoints passed, 1 for behavioral failure/no trials, 2 for blocked/error.&quot;,
  &quot;verification&quot;: &quot;tests/test_research_eval.py&quot;
}</pre></article><h2>Experiment history</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Experiment</th><th>Mode</th><th>Outcome</th><th>Checks</th><th>Seconds</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Existing suite baseline</td><td></td><td>55 passed, 1 opt-in live Codex test skipped</td><td>Unscored</td><td>8.83</td></tr><tr><td>New adversarial regression baseline</td><td></td><td>8 failed</td><td>Unscored</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>baseline-connected-01/buried-bottleneck</td><td>live-autonomous</td><td>paused</td><td>0/8</td><td>10.874</td></tr><tr><td>baseline-live-01/buried-bottleneck</td><td>live-autonomous</td><td>error</td><td>Unscored</td><td>1.521</td></tr><tr><td>harness-01/buried-bottleneck</td><td>scripted-harness-only</td><td>completed</td><td>8/8</td><td>0.622</td></tr><tr><td>harness-01/negative-control</td><td>scripted-harness-only</td><td>completed</td><td>8/8</td><td>0.623</td></tr><tr><td>live-01/buried-bottleneck</td><td>live-autonomous</td><td>error</td><td>Unscored</td><td>1.398</td></tr><tr><td>live-02/negative-control</td><td>live-autonomous</td><td>error</td><td>Unscored</td><td>1.387</td></tr><tr><td>live-connected-01/buried-bottleneck</td><td>live-autonomous</td><td>paused</td><td>0/8</td><td>12.558</td></tr><tr><td>live-connected-02/negative-control</td><td>live-autonomous</td><td>active</td><td>3/8</td><td>57.432</td></tr><tr><td>live-iteration-02/buried-bottleneck</td><td>live-autonomous</td><td>paused</td><td>0/8</td><td>26.6</td></tr><tr><td>live-iteration-03/buried-bottleneck</td><td>live-autonomous</td><td>paused</td><td>0/8</td><td>7.391</td></tr><tr><td>live-iteration-04/buried-bottleneck</td><td>live-autonomous</td><td>completed</td><td>6/8</td><td>39.711</td></tr><tr><td>live-iteration-05/buried-bottleneck</td><td>live-autonomous</td><td>completed</td><td>5/8</td><td>23.581</td></tr><tr><td>live-negative-04/negative-control</td><td>live-autonomous</td><td>completed</td><td>5/8</td><td>27.945</td></tr><tr><td>live-negative-05/negative-control</td><td>live-auton